`contracts/formats.md` §주제 사전 v3 의 판정 원장과 맞댄다 (포크 #56).

Writing df into the ledger without leaving the way to measure it makes that number quietly false the
moment the corpus grows (the same place as `tool/measure-evidence-fixture` in #6 and
`tool/measure-crosscheck-keys` in #7).

**The counting rule is exactly the dictionary's matching rule** -- `ko` is a substring (case
insensitive) and `latin` is a boundary match (`analysis/retrieval/topics.py`). Mixing the two rules
splits the number: `sunscreen` is 81 as a substring and 76 on boundaries, and those five of difference
are the plural `sunscreens`. The dictionary matches on boundaries, so the ledger's number is 76.

Three numbers are given. **Because df alone cannot decide a listing** -- if an alias that is already
there sees every one of those documents, the new row observes nothing
있으면 새 행은 아무것도 관측하지 않는다(`톤업크림` 628 편 전부를 `톤업` 이 이미 본다).

  df       the number of documents the surface appears in
  new      documents where the surface appears but **the topic at that place cannot see it without this
           row** (= what the row newly observes)
  unseen   documents where the surface appears but **no topic catches it without these rows** (= a hole
           in the dictionary)

The baseline dictionary for the last two numbers is **the dictionary with every ledger surface taken
out**. Using the load source as it is makes `new` all 0 after a listing, so "what does this row
observe" can no longer be asked again.

What is red (exit code 1 = do not trust this output).

  floor    a listed surface has fallen below `terms.MIN_DOCS`. The ground for listing it has collapsed.
  idle     a listed surface has `new` 0 while the ledger wrote that it is not 0 (or the other way round).
  revived  an unlisted surface passed the floor and gained `new` as well. Time to judge it again.

    tool/measure-lexicon-candidates                        # the human-readable table
    tool/measure-lexicon-candidates --json                 # the form the tests read
    tool/measure-lexicon-candidates --corpus <document.csv>
"""

